{"id":"cloud","name":"Cloud","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:cloud"],"groups":["Appearances Of"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Cloud","text":"The Hebrew so rendered means “a covering,” because clouds cover the sky. The word is used as a symbol of the Divine presence, as indicating the splendour of that glory which it conceals (Ex. 16:10; 33:9; Num. 11:25; 12:5; Job 22:14; Ps. 18:11). A “cloud without rain” is a proverbial saying, denoting a man who does not keep his promise (Prov. 16:15; Isa. 18:4; 25:5; Jude 1:12). A cloud is the figure of that which is transitory (Job 30:15; Hos. 6:4). A bright cloud is the symbolical seat of the Divine presence (Ex. 29:42, 43; 1 Kings 8:10; 2 Chr. 5:14; Ezek. 43:4), and was called the Shechinah (q.v.). Jehovah came down upon Sinai in a cloud (Ex. 19:9); and the cloud filled the court around the tabernacle in the wilderness so that Moses could not enter it (Ex. 40:34, 35). At the dedication of the temple also the cloud “filled the house of the Lord” (1 Kings 8:10). Thus in like manner when …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H6051","lemma":"עָנָן","xlit":"ʻânân","gloss":"a cloud","kjv":"cloud","count":45,"share":0.67},{"strong":"H3519","lemma":"כָּבוֹד","xlit":"kâbôwd","gloss":"weight, but only figuratively in a good sense, splendor","kjv":"glorious, glory, honour","count":16,"share":0.24},{"strong":"H5265","lemma":"נָסַע","xlit":"nâçaʻ","gloss":"to pull up, especially the tent-pins","kjv":"cause to blow, bring, get, go","count":14,"share":0.21},{"strong":"H784","lemma":"אֵשׁ","xlit":"ʼêsh","gloss":"fire","kjv":"burning, fiery, fire, flaming","count":15,"share":0.22},{"strong":"H3119","lemma":"יוֹמָם","xlit":"yôwmâm","gloss":"daily","kjv":"daily, day","count":10,"share":0.15},{"strong":"H3915","lemma":"לַיִל","xlit":"layil","gloss":"a twist","kjv":"night","count":12,"share":0.18}],"verses":["Exod.13.21","Exod.13.22","Exod.14.19","Exod.14.24","Exod.16.10","Exod.19.9","Exod.19.16","Exod.24.16","Exod.24.18","E